HST PDF: the visible signature box in the style of administrative documents - signer, organisation,
signing time with UTC offset and reason in black serif text on white, the font shrinking until the
wrapped lines fit the box.

The box used to size its font for two or three lines (6 to 11 pt) from the box height alone; a long
signer name or reason wraps to more lines and then ran past the box. Its fields now follow the
signed administrative documents (Nghị định 30/2020) and the CA signing tools:

    Ký bởi: <common name>
    Cơ quan: <organisation, when the certificate has one that differs from the common name>
    Thời gian ký: dd/mm/yyyy hh:mm:ss +07:00
    Lý do: <reason, when given>

- pdfviewersigning createAppearance: the fields above in black on white inside a 0.5 pt dark grey
  frame; the largest font from 10 down to 5 pt at which the wrapped text fits, fixed 6/3 pt
  padding. No "valid" tick is drawn: only a PDF reader's check can say that.
- serifFamily: Liberation Serif (bundled on every platform, Times New Roman metrics, full Vietnamese,
  embeddable), else Noto Serif, Times New Roman, DejaVu Serif - the first that is installed and has
  every glyph of the text, so the PDF writer embeds it rather than a silent substitute.
- describeCertificate: CertificateDescription::aOrganisation from the subject's O.
- strings.hrc / vi messages.po: "Signed by", "Organization", "Signing time" (Ký bởi, Cơ quan, Thời gian
  ký).

